      "extract": "We will write use standard notation, such as $\\partial X$ and $\\mathrm{int}(X)$ for the boundary and the interior of a subset $X$ of the complex plane ${\\mathbb C}$. The complex conjugate of a complex number $z$ is usually written as $\\bar z$. We write ${\\mathbb R}$ for the real line, ${\\mathbb D}:=\\{z\\in{\\mathbb C}:|z|<1\\}$ for the open unit disk, and ${\\mathbb D}^e:=\\{z\\in{\\mathbb C}:|z|>1\\}$ for the open exterior",
