      "extract": "[]{#sec-polybargmann label=\"sec-polybargmann\"} We will consider the Bargmann-Fock space $A^2_{m,q}({\\mathbb C})$ of poly-analytic functions of degree $\\le q-1$, i.e., functions of the form $$f(z) = \\sum_{r=0}^{q-1} \\bar{z}^r f_r(z),$$ where all the components $f_r$ are entire, subject to the norm integrability condition $$\\|f\\|^2_{A^2_{m,q}({\\mathbb C})}:= \\|f\\|^2_{L^2({\\mathbb C},\\mathrm e^{-m|z|^2})}",
      "extractCut": true
    },
