      "extract": "In this section, we discuss the poly-Bargmann transforms, a generalization of the classical Bargmann transform, which are needed later when we analyze the Berezin density at a boundary point. The poly-Bargmann transforms appeared in Vasilevski's paper [@vas], where the basic properties were presented. We denote by $H_j$ the $j$-th Hermite polynomial with respect to the Gaussian weight $\\mathrm e^{-\\frac12t^2}$",
